KG42.register("source_edge_archive-bb61ce263844cdb0141bbb62",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R011::E::v141-c-R011-E001","paper":"05-double_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","rule_ref":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R011","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-69ba805a251afd65","target":"COMP-6057789601b08e93","source_occurrence_id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R011::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"05-double_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"05-double_auction::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Financial balance of discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller transactions. | Winning buyer-seller pairs in discriminatory k-DA local energy transactions; prices are pair-specific rather than uniform across the auction interval.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g01-ev-10"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"34cd6d78259e53c9cbbd95cba655687b3edabb9f1f090e6f817ec0bcec1a3cce","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Each qualifying winning buyer-seller pair pays k times its own buyer bid plus (1-k) times its own seller ask, with bid at least ask and fixed k in [0,1]. There is no common auction-interval price; the source Pay-as-Bid label is not a pure own-bid payment identity.","target_definition":"Monetary obligations, transfers, sharing or settlement conditions in this mechanism: Sealed bid/ask natural ordering; each winning pair trades at k times its buyer bid plus (1-k) times its seller ask; no common interval price.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Each winning pair's local transaction price determines both the buyer's payment rate and the seller's receipt rate as kB^P + (1 - k)S^P. Scope: Winning buyer-seller pairs in discriminatory k-DA local energy transactions; prices are pair-specific rather than uniform across the auction interval. Condition: B^P ≥ S^P; k is predetermined in [0, 1].","expression":"\\text{price trading buyers pay} = \\text{price trading sellers receive} = k B^P + (1-k) S^P, \\quad B^P \\geq S^P,\\ k \\in [0,1]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R011-x-BP","v141-c-R011-x-SP"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R011-theta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-01","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"he presented in this paper. es lt u- 2.1. Review of auction mechanims er er While a multitude of mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In Discriminatory k-DA [46], otherwise known as Pay-as-Bid k-Double Auction, buyers submit sealed bid prices $B^P$ while sellers submit sealed ask prices $S^P$. Following the natural ordering rule, bid prices are sorted in a descending order while ask prices are sorted in an ascending order. If $B^P \\geq S^P$, a trade occurs at the listed price in Table 1 where $k$ is a predetermined constant in the closed interval [0, 1]. Since the trading price is determined between each winning buyer-seller pair, the described mechanism is discriminatory. A single market clearing price does not exist for each auction interval."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-03","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 1 Auction mechanisms. Discriminatory k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB^P + (1 - k)S^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB^P + (1 - k)S^P$"}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Financial balance of discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller transactions. | Winning buyer-seller pairs in discriminatory k-DA local energy transactions; prices are pair-specific rather than uniform across the auction interval.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g01-ev-10"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]},"paper_scope_note":"The four auctions are kept separate; the time-period conditions of marginal index, buy/sell eligibility, price bound, shortfall subsidy, and historical price are retained. What is cited is the mechanism description given in the paper and is not expanded to all VCG definitions."}});
